  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment of the Impact of the Syrian War and Refugee Crisis on Trafficking in Persons (AIS-TIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPD is assessing the impact of the Syrian war and refugee crisis on trafficking in persons in Syria and the surrounding region (which may include Jordan, Lebanon, Iraq, Turkey, and Syria). The project will produce a comprehensive research report, to-be presented to the Department for public use, detailing and analyzing this impact in Syria and the neighboring countries, and will include feasible recommendations to respond to the research findings. The assessment will contribute to a strengthened response to human trafficking by relevant actors operating in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
